': coded C + prongs + height, e.g. C4L = 4 prongs, low (L low / M mid / H high). More prongs resist breaking; higher cores strike higher but are less stable.',
': the bottom part touching the floor, which decides how the top moves. When the gear around the tip grips the stadium\'s "drive rail", it triggers a ',
