'Launch rules', 'Only launch when the countdown "3, 2, 1, FIGHT!" reaches "FIGHT!".', 'Launching too early or too late is a ', 'launch fault', '. The first fault in a match is a warning; ', 'a second fault gives the opponent 1 point', ', then both relaunch.',
'The faster you pull the cord, the higher the starting spin. You can aim the launch toward the centre or the outer rail.',
'Every edge ring has its own special move. It charges automatically during battle, faster with impacts and rail dashes.',
'When charged, press ', 'Space', ' or the special button to unleash it — once per round.',
'Each player registers 3 tops; each round uses slots 1 → 2 → 3 in order, then cycles.',
'Within one deck, ', 'each part can only be used once', ' (no two identical edge rings, lock cores or spin tips).',
'If both tops finish at the same moment (e.g. both stop), it is a draw: no points, and both relaunch.',
